menu "Wireless (BLE MIDI)"

config SYNTH_WIRELESS
	bool "Wireless support (BLE MIDI in)"
	depends on BT_ENABLED && BT_NIMBLE_ENABLED
	default n
	help
		On-demand BLE MIDI input: a "Wireless" menu page starts a NimBLE
		peripheral session (advertises the BLE-MIDI GATT service) and tears
		it down again, returning the stack's RAM. Incoming notes play a
		dedicated live synth slot. When disabled, no radio code is compiled
		and the menu entry does not exist.

		Requires the NimBLE host (Component config -> Bluetooth), trimmed to
		peripheral-only so the stack costs as little internal RAM as it can:
		BT_NIMBLE_ROLE_CENTRAL=n, BT_NIMBLE_ROLE_OBSERVER=n,
		BT_NIMBLE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=1, BT_NIMBLE_GATT_SERVER=y. Pin both stack
		halves to core 0 (BT_NIMBLE_PINNED_TO_CORE_0, BT_CTRL_PINNED_TO_CORE_0)
		to keep them off the AMY render core.

config SYNTH_BLE_MIDI_LOG
	bool "Verbose BLE MIDI logging"
	depends on SYNTH_WIRELESS
	default n
	help
		Logs per-packet BLE MIDI traffic details. Diagnostic only: the log
		calls sit on the NimBLE host task in the note path, so keep this
		off outside debugging sessions.

endmenu
